From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 18:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] data: alarm vibration with the priority of an alert
Description:
 The vibration of alarm-clock-elapsed had no priority, unlike its sound
 and the other alerts. It used priority 0: any other vibration, a new
 message included, ended it, and while one ran the alarm did not vibrate.
 Give it priority 192 like the incoming call.
Author: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-28
---
diff --git a/data/default.json b/data/default.json
index 600ea79..a3335f6 100644
--- a/data/default.json
+++ b/data/default.json
@@ -116,6 +116,7 @@
       "feedbacks" : [
         {
           "event-name"   : "alarm-clock-elapsed",
+          "priority"     : 192,
           "type"         : "VibraPeriodic",
           "magnitude"    : 0.5,
           "duration"     : 1000
